---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import Workflow from '../components/Workflow.astro';
import { faqs } from '../content/site';
---
<SiteLayout title="OurPort | Smart lockers for wash-and-fold laundry" description="Plan a laundry drop-off and pickup point for your laundromat, apartment community or student residence. OurPort, powered by Monetize That.">
  <section class="container home-hero">
    <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Smart lockers. Laundry first.</p><h1>A better place <br /> for laundry <br /> <span>to change hands.</span></h1><p class="hero-description">Controlled drop-off and pickup for wash-and-fold. Planned around your space, your service, and the people who use it.</p><a class="button" href="/plan-a-site/">Discuss fit and pricing <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="audience-links"><a href="/laundromats/">For laundromats <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/housing/">For apartments & student housing <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
    <figure class="hero-figure"><div class="image-frame"><img src="/images/laundromat-wall.webp" width="1448" height="1086" alt="Proposed OurPort laundry locker wall within a bright laundromat, with machines and clear circulation space." fetchpriority="high" /><span class="image-label">A wall with more to offer.</span></div><figcaption><span>Indoor laundry wall</span><span>Illustrative concept</span></figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <section class="promise-bar"><div class="container"><span>Wash-and-fold drop-off & pickup</span><span>Indoor, site-led configurations</span><span>Your operator. Your customer relationship.</span></div></section>
  <section class="container information-band" aria-label="What OurPort coordinates">
    <div class="information-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The service point, considered as a whole</p><h2>Hardware is one part of the handoff.</h2><p>OurPort brings the physical wall, laundry workflow and site requirements into one practical conversation.</p></div>
    <div class="information-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Service</h3><p>Who accepts, prices, processes and supports each order.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Access</h3><p>When customers and staff can reach the lockers—and what happens when they cannot.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Systems</h3><p>Order status, payment, notifications and the existing dashboard that must stay useful.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Site</h3><p>Bag fit, wall dimensions, circulation, power, network and optional monitoring.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container audience-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Two places to start</p><h2>One handoff. <br /> Different possibilities.</h2></div><p>Bring laundry service closer to daily life—at the place it is processed, or the place people call home.</p></div><div class="audience-grid"><a class="audience-card" href="/laundromats/"><div class="card-image"><img src="/images/laundromat-wall.webp" width="1448" height="1086" alt="Illustrative laundry service wall inside a laundromat." loading="lazy" /></div><div class="audience-card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">For laundromats</span><h3>Make the wall work another shift.</h3><p>Give customers another way to leave and collect orders, while your team controls pricing, processing and service.</p><span class="text-link">Explore the laundromat wall <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a><a class="audience-card" href="/housing/"><div class="card-image"><img src="/images/housing-lobby.webp" width="1672" height="941" alt="Illustrative OurPort locker cabinet in a residential entry lobby." loading="lazy" /></div><div class="audience-card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">For apartments & student housing</span><h3>Laundry service, closer to home.</h3><p>Create a convenient collection point for residents and their laundry provider, with the property’s access rules in place.</p><span class="text-link">Explore the resident amenity <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a></div></section>
  <Workflow />
  <section class="section container fit-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">Designed around the handoff</p><h2>The bag. <br /> The people. <br /> The place.</h2><p>A useful locker starts with the things that go inside it—and the work around it.</p></div><div class="numbered-features"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Start with a full laundry bag.</h3><p>Confirm the incoming load and finished bundle fit the clear door opening. Then choose the compartment mix.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Keep the operation connected.</h3><p>Map your existing dashboard, staff handoffs and customer notifications before confirming the software setup.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Make it belong in the room.</h3><p>Plan placement, access, power and connectivity together. Explore a fitted wall or repeatable locker bays.</p></div></article></div></section>
  <section class="section planning-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">From idea to a site plan</p><h2>A clear path to a credible configuration.</h2></div><p>Early questions are useful. They prevent a generic cabinet from becoming a promise the room or operation cannot support.</p></div><ol class="planning-steps"><li><span class="planning-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◎</span><div><small>01</small><strong>Describe the operation</strong><p>Audience, location, service, hours and current software.</p></div></li><li><span class="planning-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↔</span><div><small>02</small><strong>Measure the handoff</strong><p>Full bag, finished return, available wall and access route.</p></div></li><li><span class="planning-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◇</span><div><small>03</small><strong>Define responsibilities</strong><p>Operator, property, customer support, network and exceptions.</p></div></li><li><span class="planning-symbol" aria-hidden="true">▦</span><div><small>04</small><strong>Price the configuration</strong><p>Cabinet mix, controls, installation and recurring services.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
  <section class="section faq-section"><div class="container faq-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">A few practical answers</p><h2>Before we <br /> plan your site.</h2></div><div class="faq-list">{faqs.map(item => <details><summary>{item.question}<span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>{item.answer}</p></details>)}</div></div></section>
  <CallToAction />
</SiteLayout>
